label("$2x+3$",(4.5,12.5),W);
[/asy]

solution:
We apply the distributive property repeatedly:

\begin{align*}
(x+10)(2y+10) &= x(2y+10) + 10(2y+10)\\
&= x\cdot 2y + x\cdot 10 + 10\cdot 2y + 10\cdot 10\\
&= \boxed{2xy + 10x + 20y + 100}.
\end{align*}

We have the equation $\frac{3+x}{5+x}=\frac{1+x}{2+x}$. Simplifying, we get \begin{align*}
(3+x)(2+x)&=(5+x)(1+x)\\
6+5x+x^2&=5+6x+x^2\\
x&=\boxed{1}.
\end{align*}

